---
import FlowDetail from '../FlowDetail.astro';
import detailToolbarPreview from '../../../assets/flow/details/detail-toolbar-preview.webp';
import detailResult from '../../../assets/flow/details/detail-result.webp';
import detailDiff from '../../../assets/flow/details/detail-diff.webp';
---
<section class="px-6 py-16 sm:py-24" aria-labelledby="tour-agency">
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-6xl">
    <div class="max-w-3xl">
      <p class="of-eyebrow" data-animate="rise">Agency</p>
      <h3 id="tour-agency" class="of-display scroll-mt-28 mt-4 text-[clamp(1.85rem,3.4vw,2.75rem)]" data-animate="lead">One path from request to approved change.</h3>
      <p class="of-lede mt-5" data-animate="rise">
        Proofread, Summarize, Translate, two table conversions, Expand with Sources, and
        Visualize all use the same trust path. Flow states the scope, route, and cost first.
        The result arrives as a review. The file changes only after you approve it.
      </p>
    </div>
    <ol class="flow-path mt-12" data-animate-stagger="slow">
      <li class="flow-path__step" data-animate="rise">
        <div class="flow-path__copy">
          <p class="flow-path__num">Before</p>
          <h4 class="flow-path__head">Know the bargain before the run.</h4>
          <p class="flow-path__body">Hover an action to see what text it will use, what it should cost, which model will run, and whether the text leaves your Mac.</p>
        </div>
        <FlowDetail src={detailToolbarPreview} alt="Flow's document tool strip with Proofread open, showing the document scope, no cost, and the local model that would run." caption="Scope, cost, model, and locality · Before the click" sizes="(min-width: 900px) 38rem, calc(100vw - 3rem)" />
      </li>
      <li class="flow-path__step" data-animate="rise">
        <div class="flow-path__copy">
          <p class="flow-path__num">Review</p>
          <h4 class="flow-path__head">Judge the writing. Inspect the bytes.</h4>
          <p class="flow-path__body">Flow opens on the proposed document with the change highlighted. Exact changes, evidence, and named checks stay one tab away.</p>
        </div>
        <FlowDetail src={detailResult} alt="Flow's review pane on the proposed document, scrolled to a corrected sentence with the changed words highlighted." caption="The result first · Exact changes one tab away" sizes="(min-width: 900px) 38rem, calc(100vw - 3rem)" />
      </li>
      <li class="flow-path__step" data-animate="rise">
        <div class="flow-path__copy">
          <p class="flow-path__num">Approve</p>
          <h4 class="flow-path__head">Your review unlocks the save.</h4>
          <p class="flow-path__body">Approve &amp; Save stays disabled until you confirm the review. Reject changes nothing. A byte guard stops an older run from landing over newer work.</p>
        </div>
        <FlowDetail src={detailDiff} alt="Flow's decision footer with a human-review checkbox and a disabled Approve and Save button beside Reject and Later." caption="Nothing saved until you approve · Reject changes nothing" sizes="(min-width: 900px) 38rem, calc(100vw - 3rem)" glow />
      </li>
    </ol>
  </div>
</section>
